        "original_id": "49145b6c-b1f0-575f-8f81-cd85e65fb2bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Hyatt New York, Grand Central Terminal, Midtown Manhattan, New York City\n- Products: Commodore Hotel\n- People: Donald Trump, John Steber\n- Events: 1945 NFL Draft\n- Organizations: National Football League, United States\n- Roles: President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Commodore Hotel in New York City was originally built and opened on January 28, 1919.\n- The 1945 National Football League Draft was held on April 8, 1945, at the Commodore Hotel in New York City.\n- John Steber was drafted in the seventh round with the 61st overall pick of the 1945 National Football League Draft.\n- Donald Trump was born on June 14, 1946.\n- In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the exterior of the Commodore Hotel building and renovated its interior as his first construction project in Manhattan.\n- The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel located directly east of Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.\n- Donald Trump became the 45th President of the United States on January 20, 2017 and is described as the current president.",
